   "text": "This is tylosin (a 16-membered macrolide), and I wrote the SMILES from memory of its standard form rather than deriving each stereocentre from the wedges. I checked the connectivity against the drawing, but not each wedge and hash individually.\n\n**Macrolactone ring**, in order around the ring:\n- The ring oxygen is attached to the ethyl-bearing carbon, which is followed by the carbon carrying the CH2\u2013O\u2013sugar group.\n- Next comes CH=C(CH3)\u2013CH=CH\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH2, a diene-one with a methyl on the diene.\n- The ring then reaches CH(CH2CHO), whose side chain is the aldehyde, then CH(O\u2013sugar), then CH(CH3), then CH(OH), then CH2, and finally the lactone C(=O) closing back to the ring oxygen.\n\n**Left sugar** (on the CH2\u2013O side chain): a 6-deoxy sugar with two OMe groups and one OH, the 2,3-di-O-methyl-6-deoxyhexose mycinose.\n\n**Right sugars**, on the ring CH\u2013O:\n- The first is a 6-deoxy sugar bearing NMe2 and OH, which is mycaminose.\n- It carries a second sugar on its 4-O, a 2,6-dideoxy sugar with a C-methyl and OH groups, which is mycarose.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@@H]1[C@H](/C=C(/C=C/C(=O)[C@@H](C[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H](CC(=O)O1)O)C)O[C@H]2[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O2)C)O[C@H]3C[C@@]([C@H]([C@@H](O3)C)O)(C)O)N(C)C)O)CC=O)C)/C)CO[C@H]4[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O4)C)O)OC)OC"
